------------------------   PROJECT 4 - INDIVIDUAL   ------------------------

RUNNING THE SIMULATION
    1) Download and open the following files:
             o   init_Track.m
             o   init_Car.m
             o   Main.m
             o   AnimateTrack.m
             o   Actual_Animation.m
             o   raceStat.m
             o   P4_Wk3.slx
    2) Run the following file:
             o   Main.m

PROJECT SUMMARY

This part of the project works on our base model used throughout Project 4 that had us
combining lateral and longitudinal dynamics and a driver model to guide a car with an 
EV based powertrain around the track. We suppose to have the vehicle go around the track
as many times as possible in 1 hour starting at an 80% SOC and utilizing regenerative 
breaking along the way. We failed to get the vehicle to complete a whole lap, but from
the base I added a Height subsystem that took in the X-position of the track in order
to identify its location. It then uses the given formula to solve for the height of the
race track and thus the angle of the slope that the car has to face while going up this 
slope. From this it adds a force that will take the slope into account using the force
due to gravity relation or F = m*g*sin(theta). Then subtracting this from the net forces
in the longitudinal forces subsystem that is used to find acceleration, the system accounts
for the difference in height that takes place.

